Objectives
•Collect real-time temperature, humidity and light-intensity readings with a DHT11 and a BH1750
sensor.
•Connect the microcontroller to Wi-Fi and upload readings to Firebase every 10 seconds with
timestamps.
•Keep a history of all sensor readings in the cloud.
•Build a responsive dashboard with live graphs, device online/offline status and an LED ON/OFF
button.
•Raise an alert (buzzer and dashboard message) when the temperature exceeds a user-defined
threshold.
2. Project Impact
The system gives a low-cost way to watch the conditions of a room from anywhere with an internet
connection, and to react quickly when conditions go outside a safe limit.
•Remote monitoring: readings can be seen on any phone or computer browser, without being
near the device.
•Early warning: the buzzer and the dashboard alert warn the user when the temperature crosses
the threshold they set.
•Data for decisions: stored history shows trends in temperature, humidity and light, which helps
in comfort control, storage conditions and planning.
•Energy awareness: light-level readings can support decisions about switching lights on or off.
•Low cost and scalable: the parts are inexpensive, and more sensors or devices can be added to
the same database.
•Practical learning: the project covers embedded programming, cloud databases and web
development in one system.
